# Voicemail Greeting Generator - Cursor Rules

## Project Information

- Project: Voicemail Greeting Generator
- Stack: Next.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Hosting: Vercel
- TTS Provider: Cartesia API (formerly used ElevenLabs)
- Audio Processing: FFmpeg
- Storage: Vercel Blob Storage

## Development Rules

- Use TypeScript for all new components and functions
- Follow existing component patterns when adding new features
- Keep environment variables in .env file (don't commit sensitive keys)
- Test audio generation locally before deploying
- Maintain the existing UI design language with Tailwind CSS
- Use Vercel Blob for file storage instead of local filesystem
- Never write directly to server disk in production

## API Keys

- Cartesia API: Used for text-to-speech generation
- Vercel Blob: perfectgreet_READ_WRITE_TOKEN for file storage
- Never expose API keys in client-side code

## Core Features

- Text-to-speech voicemail/hold message generation
- Background music integration
- Voice selection with various accents
- MP3 download functionality
- Serverless audio file storage

## Project Structure Notes

- src/app - Next.js 13+ app directory structure
- src/components - Reusable UI components
- src/app/api - API routes for voice generation
- output/ - Only for local development (use Vercel Blob in production)

# Blog Post Generation Guide

## Directory Structure

```
src/
├── posts/           # Markdown files for blog posts
└── public/
    └── posts/       # Generated thumbnails for blog posts
```

## Step 1: Create New Blog Post

1. Create a new markdown file in `src/posts/` with the format:

   - Filename: `your-post-title.md`
   - Use kebab-case for the filename
   - Example: `how-to-create-professional-voicemail.md`

2. Use this frontmatter template at the top of your markdown file:

```markdown
---
title: Your Post Title
date: "YYYY-MM-DD"
image: "/posts/your-post-title.png"
description: A compelling description of your post in one sentence.
---

---

Your content starts here...
```

## Step 2: Generate Thumbnail

1. Make sure you have the required environment variable:

   ```bash
   GEMINI_API_KEY=your_api_key
   ```

2. Run the thumbnail generator script:
   ```bash
   npm run generate-thumbnail "Your Post Title"
   ```
   This will:
   - Generate a thumbnail using Gemini AI
   - Save it to `/public/posts/` with kebab-case naming
   - Match the image path in your post's frontmatter

## Step 3: Blog Post Structure

Follow this content structure for consistency:

1. **Introduction**

   - Hook the reader
   - State the problem/need
   - Preview the solution

2. **Main Content**

   - Use clear H2 (##) headings for main sections
   - Use H3 (###) for subsections
   - Include code blocks with triple backticks for scripts/examples
   - Use bullet points for lists
   - Include relevant examples

3. **Best Practices Section**

   - Include actionable tips
   - Use numbered lists for steps
   - Add implementation advice

4. **Conclusion**
   - Summarize key points
   - Include call-to-action to Perfect Greet
   - Use this template:
   ```markdown
   Ready to [benefit statement]? Visit [Perfect Greet](https://perfectgreet.site) to create free, high-quality voicemail greetings that [value proposition].
   ```

## Style Guide

1. **Formatting**

   - Use markdown for all formatting
   - Double space between sections
   - Single space between paragraphs
   - Use bold (\*\*) for emphasis
   - Use backticks (`) for technical terms

2. **Code Blocks**

   - Use triple backticks for voicemail scripts
   - Indent lists properly
   - Include placeholder text in [brackets]

3. **Lists**
   - Use hyphen (-) for unordered lists
   - Use numbers (1.) for ordered lists
   - Indent sublists with 2 spaces

